---
title: Styles
description: The Tailwind v4 design tokens that power the docs shell and every published component.
order: 2
---

Every color, radius, and font in this project is a CSS custom property defined in `src/lib/styles/app.css`. Components consume them through Tailwind's semantic utilities (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`) instead of hardcoded values, so retheming the whole system means editing one file.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "tw-animate-css";
@import "shadcn-svelte/tailwind.css";
@import "@fontsource-variable/inter";

:root {
  --background: oklch(1 0 0);
  --foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
  --primary: oklch(0.205 0 0);
  /* ...card, popover, secondary, muted, accent, destructive, border, ring, chart-*, sidebar-* */
  --radius: 0.625rem;
}
```

## Light and dark

`.dark` redefines the same custom properties with an inverted palette. Dark mode is toggled by adding/removing the `dark` class on `<html>` — see the theme toggle in the docs header.

## Accent colors

Three accent presets ship out of the box, switched with a `data-accent` attribute on `<html>`:

```css
:root[data-accent="amber"] { --primary: oklch(0.66 0.19 41); /* ... */ }
:root[data-accent="violet"] { --primary: oklch(0.54 0.25 293); /* ... */ }
```

Default (no attribute) uses the neutral `--primary` defined in `:root`. Each accent also has a `.dark` variant.

## Mapping tokens into Tailwind

The `@theme inline` block maps each custom property to a Tailwind color/radius utility (`--color-primary: var(--primary)`, `--radius-lg: var(--radius)`, and so on), which is what makes `bg-primary` and `rounded-lg` resolve to the tokens above.

## Using this in your own project

Install the [`styles`](/utilities/styles) registry item. It publishes the CSS in `registry/items/files/styles` (`globals.css` plus the default, secondary, and tertiary theme presets) into `src/lib/styles/`. Import `globals.css` once from your root layout:

```svelte
<script>
  import "$lib/styles/globals.css";
</script>
```

Do this before installing components, so the semantic classes they use resolve correctly. See [Theming](/docs/theming) for how to override tokens.
